  "problem": "Evaluate $\\sqrt[3]{8a+1}$ at $a=10.$",
  "worked_solution": "We replace $a$ with $10$ in the given expression, and simplify as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{8a+1} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{8\\cdot 10+1} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{80+1} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{81} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{27\\cdot 3} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{3}^{3}\\cdot 3} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{3}^{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt[3]{3} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
